#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:3
msgid "Manage installed apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:5
msgid ""
"List, upgrade, and remove the apps pipx manages, then confirm each change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:9
msgid "List apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:11
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:84
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:120
msgid "$ pipx list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:15
msgid ""
"The output shows each package version, its apps, and the environment paths. "
"Narrow or reshape it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:17
msgid "``pipx list --short`` prints package names and versions only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:18
msgid ""
"``pipx list --include-injected`` also lists packages injected into each "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:19
msgid "``pipx list --outdated`` lists environments with an available upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:20
msgid "``pipx list --pinned`` lists pinned environments only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:24
msgid "Upgrade one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:26
msgid "$ pipx upgrade black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:30
msgid ""
"Add ``--include-injected`` to upgrade injected packages alongside the main "
"app. Pass ``--install`` to install the package spec when it is missing "
"rather than error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:33
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:50
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:66
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:82
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:101
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:118
msgid "Verify:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:35
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:68
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:103
msgid "$ pipx list --short"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:41
msgid "Upgrade all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:43
msgid "$ pipx upgrade-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:47
msgid ""
"Use ``--skip PKG ...`` to leave named environments untouched, and ``--"
"include-injected`` to include injected packages. Pinned environments are "
"skipped; see :doc:`pin-packages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:52
msgid "$ pipx list --outdated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:58
msgid "Uninstall one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:60
msgid "$ pipx uninstall black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:64
msgid "pipx deletes the environment and unlinks its apps and manual pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:74
msgid "Uninstall all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:76
msgid "$ pipx uninstall-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:80
msgid ""
"Record what you have first with ``pipx list --short`` if you plan to "
"reinstall later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:90
msgid "Reinstall one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:92
msgid ""
"Rebuild an environment from its recorded metadata, keeping the same options "
"as the original install. Reach for it after a Python upgrade or to repair a "
"broken environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:95
msgid "$ pipx reinstall black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:99
msgid "Pass ``--python`` to rebuild under another interpreter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:109
msgid "Reinstall all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:111
msgid "$ pipx reinstall-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:115
msgid ""
"Common after installing a new Python version so every app moves to it. Use "
"``--python`` to target a specific interpreter and ``--skip PKG ...`` to "
"exclude environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:126
msgid ""
"To check environments without changing them, or to repair only the broken "
"ones, see :ref:`repair-environments`."
msgstr ""
